<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_e370588e-392e-44f5-a852-647545c92b1d"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Leave to sue required for persons convicted of serious
indictable offences</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person who is in custody as a result of having
been convicted of, or found to have committed, a serious indictable offence
may not institute any civil proceedings in any court except by the leave of
that court granted on application.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Am 1999 No 94,
Sch 4.111 [2].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_685e9ce3-45bd-4a12-8dd3-d59684ab1fa4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_8e9bb34f-b692-4b9c-b17b-17b12f0aa6d9"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Grant of leave</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A court shall not, under section 4, grant leave
to a person to institute proceedings unless the court is satisfied that the
proceedings are not an abuse of process and that there is prima facie ground
for the proceedings.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ad13fd81-fc7c-4f57-b44a-d84cd5e80503"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_83b57e5b-7514-4170-a4c9-1a5698b97767"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Refusal of leave&#8212;appeal</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4ebd84c0-fc49-4f7d-910a-933b28a67b56"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to subsection (2), a person to whom leave
referred to in section 4 has been refused may appeal against the refusal as if
the decision to refuse the leave were a decision on a point of
law.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_479892fd-e290-447d-a7ea-e76a57b2f7f5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An appeal shall not lie to the Court of Appeal
(within the meaning of the <legref type="act" jurisd="NSW" check="unknown"
refid="act-1970-052"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Supreme Court Act
1970</i></name></legref>) from an order refusing leave referred to in section
4 except by the leave of the Court of Appeal.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_091fee59-1869-46e9-9ac1-b7f0ed97adf8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_344ca71f-65a5-4548-ab65-6ece2dc5f6e8"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Right of appearance</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">At the hearing or determination of an application
or appeal under this Act, except by the leave of the court to which the
application or appeal is made:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8670c2b3-7f5f-47df-b83c-132faf79c17b" id="sec.7-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the applicant or appellant, as the case may be,
is not entitled to appear in person, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_214b8fdc-8338-4eaa-967a-70f482baed01" id="sec.7-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the person who would, if the proceedings to the
institution of which the application or appeal relates were instituted, be the
defendant in those proceedings, is not entitled to appear or be
represented.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0f0e449c-cf9b-48b0-adaf-cee1ae0f9b63"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_2a677a59-2053-42f9-bf3e-fac98df46dec"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Rules of court</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Rules of court may be made for or with respect to
the practice and procedure to be followed in relation to applications or
appeals under this Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_06140b2c-7af2-4de3-81a7-9494bde07736"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_3868bb6d-079b-4530-a269-0fd5300cc7b2"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Provisions consequent on enactment of <legref type="act"
jurisd="NSW" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes Legislation
Amendment (Sentencing) Act 1999</i></name></legref></b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_91948822-5b2f-4595-bb2e-4153b6e193b3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Section 3, as in force immediately before its
repeal by the 1999 amending Act, continues to have effect in relation to any
person who was convicted of a felony before the repeal of that
section.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e98e0eed-1b76-4b95-80bf-402a499da465"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Sections 4&#8211;7, as in force immediately
before their amendment by the 1999 amending Act, apply to a person who was
convicted of a felony before their amendment as if the person had been
convicted of a serious indictable offence.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_47802381-9924-4125-ac43-46d1dcb26db7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section, <defterm type="definition"
guid="_2bcb50cd-f090-40c7-bdd3-6d9ea371334a"
id="sec.9-ssec.3-def.1999amendingAct"><b><i>1999 amending
Act</i></b></defterm> means the <legref type="act" jurisd="NSW"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes Legislation Amendment
(Sentencing) Act 1999</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 9:</b> Ins 1999 No 94,
Sch 4.111 [3].</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


